prompt:
Validate this Normalizer transform against its metadata and requirements.

Build event expansion for the warranty payout allocation feed, applying the first matching test. Keep listed postings in order.

1) claim_type equals "DUP" means nothing, under the duplicate warranty treatment.
2) parts_cost < 0 means ERROR valued at -parts_cost, under the invalid parts treatment.
3) claim_type equals "EXPIRED" means nothing, under the expired coverage treatment.
4) claim_type equals "REPLACE" means DEVICE valued at parts_cost, then RECOVERY valued at -labour_cost, under the replacement device treatment.
5) claim_type equals "SHARED" and review means MAKER valued at (parts_cost+labour_cost)*(100-25)/100, then DEALER valued at (parts_cost+labour_cost)*25/100, then AUDIT valued at 0, under the reviewed shared liability treatment.
6) parts_cost equals 0 means LABOUR valued at labour_cost, then HANDLING valued at 2, under the labour only treatment.
7) claim_type equals "SHARED" means MAKER valued at (parts_cost+labour_cost)*(100-25)/100, then DEALER valued at (parts_cost+labour_cost)*25/100, under the shared liability treatment.
8) none of the preceding conditions applies means REPAIR valued at parts_cost+labour_cost, under the standard repair treatment.

Input 0 (In_warranty_sharing_2): external_warranty_id <required string>; claim_type <required string>; parts_cost <required decimal>; labour_cost <required decimal>; review <required boolean>; service_note <nullable string>.
Output 0 (Out_warranty_sharing_2): parent_warranty_ref <required string>; payout_leg <required string>; amount <required decimal>; allocation_key <required long>.
Each source ID is unique; carry external_warranty_id into parent_warranty_ref. Entry labels go in payout_leg, values in amount. Every nonsilent event receives a fresh allocation_key shared by its postings. Sequence Keys_warranty_sharing: long, start 3000000000, step 1, reset for this run; silent events consume no key.

```ctl
//#CTL2
string warranty_reference;
string[] warranty_actions = [];
decimal[] warranty_values = [];
long warranty_key;
function void post_warranty(string label, decimal value) {
    append(warranty_actions, label);
    append(warranty_values, value);
}
function integer count() {
    warranty_actions = [];
    warranty_values = [];
    warranty_reference = $in.0.external_warranty_id;
    warranty_key = 0L;
    /* Priority table:
       1. duplicate warranty -> 0 rows
       2. invalid parts -> 1 rows
       3. expired coverage -> 0 rows
       4. replacement device -> 2 rows
       5. reviewed shared liability -> 3 rows
       6. labour only -> 2 rows
       7. shared liability -> 2 rows
       8. standard repair -> 1 rows
    */
    if ($in.0.claim_type == "DUP") {
        return 0; // duplicate warranty
    }
    else if ($in.0.parts_cost < 0d) {
        warranty_key = sequence(Keys_warranty_sharing, long).next();
        post_warranty("ERROR", -$in.0.parts_cost);
        return 1; // invalid parts
    }
    else if ($in.0.claim_type == "EXPIRED") {
        return 0; // expired coverage
    }
    else if ($in.0.claim_type == "REPLACE") {
        warranty_key = sequence(Keys_warranty_sharing, long).next();
        post_warranty("DEVICE", $in.0.parts_cost);
        post_warranty("RECOVERY", -$in.0.labour_cost);
        return 2; // replacement device
    }
    else if ($in.0.claim_type == "SHARED" && $in.0.review) {
        warranty_key = sequence(Keys_warranty_sharing, long).next();
        post_warranty("MAKER", ($in.0.parts_cost+$in.0.labour_cost)*(100d-25d)/100d);
        post_warranty("DEALER", ($in.0.parts_cost+$in.0.labour_cost)*25d/100d);
        post_warranty("AUDIT", 0d);
        return 3; // reviewed shared liability
    }
    else if ($in.0.parts_cost == 0d) {
        warranty_key = sequence(Keys_warranty_sharing, long).next();
        post_warranty("LABOUR", $in.0.labour_cost);
        post_warranty("HANDLING", 2d);
        return 2; // labour only
    }
    else if ($in.0.claim_type == "SHARED") {
        warranty_key = sequence(Keys_warranty_sharing, long).next();
        post_warranty("MAKER", ($in.0.parts_cost+$in.0.labour_cost)*(100d-25d)/100d);
        post_warranty("DEALER", ($in.0.parts_cost+$in.0.labour_cost)*25d/100d);
        return 2; // shared liability
    }
    else if (true) {
        warranty_key = sequence(Keys_warranty_sharing, long).next();
        post_warranty("REPAIR", $in.0.parts_cost+$in.0.labour_cost);
        return 1; // standard repair
    }
    return 0;
}
function integer transform(integer idx) {
    $out.0.parent_warranty_ref = warranty_reference;
    $out.1.payout_leg = warranty_actions[idx];
    $out.0.amount = warranty_values[idx];
    $out.0.allocation_key = warranty_key;
    return ALL;
}
```

