The ExtMergeJoin action planner for scanner history. It is a left outer join: arriving scanners are on input 0, unique current dimension rows on input 1. An unseen scanner emits OPEN using its reserved key, effective start and null end. A match emits CLOSE using the existing surrogate/start and the arriving effective instant as its half-open end; a separate stage creates matched replacements. Matches are confirmed changes with effective after their old start.

Input 0 ScannerArrival(scanner:string!,effective:date!,reserved_sk:long!); input 1 ScannerCurrent(scanner:string!,sk:long!,valid_from:date!). Both inputs are ascending by scanner, joinKey $scanner#$scanner, joinType leftOuter. Output ScannerAction(scanner:string!,op:string!,sk:long!,valid_from:date!,valid_to:date?).

