Build event expansion for the media royalty settlement feed, applying the first matching test. Keep listed postings in order.

1) For withdrawn license (territory_status equals "WITHDRAWN"), the event produces nothing.
2) For negative units (licensed_units < 0), the event produces ERROR valued at -licensed_units.
3) For promotional grant (territory_status equals "PROMO"), the event produces nothing.
4) For chargeback (territory_status equals "CHARGEBACK"), the event produces CHARGEBACK valued at -unit_rate*licensed_units.
5) For audited foreign license (territory_status equals "FOREIGN" and review), the event produces NET valued at unit_rate*licensed_units*(100-25)/100, then WITHHOLD valued at unit_rate*licensed_units*25/100, then AUDIT valued at 0.
6) For zero royalty (unit_rate equals 0), the event produces ZERO valued at 0, then USAGE valued at licensed_units.
7) For foreign license (territory_status equals "FOREIGN"), the event produces NET valued at unit_rate*licensed_units*(100-25)/100, then WITHHOLD valued at unit_rate*licensed_units*25/100.
8) For domestic license (none of the preceding conditions applies), the event produces GROSS valued at unit_rate*licensed_units.

Input 0 (In_royalty_withholding_2): string[required] external_license_id; string[required] territory_status; decimal[required] unit_rate; decimal[required] licensed_units; boolean[required] review; string[nullable] license_note.
Output 0 (Out_royalty_withholding_2): string[required] parent_license_ref; string[required] royalty_leg; decimal[required] amount.
Each source ID is unique; carry external_license_id into parent_license_ref. Entry labels go in royalty_leg, values in amount.

```ctl
//#CTL2
string royalty_reference;
