The insurance endorsement postings export. Listed rules have precedence from top to bottom. Parentheses give the exact value for each named entry.

1. withdrawn: when transaction equals "WITHDRAW", export nothing.
2. invalid term: when remaining_terms <= 0 or remaining_terms > 12, export ERROR (0).
3. waiver: when transaction equals "WAIVE", export WAIVER (premium).
4. cancellation: when transaction equals "CANCEL", export REFUND (-premium*remaining_terms/12).
5. audited endorsement: when transaction equals "AMEND" and reviewed, export DEBIT (premium*remaining_terms/12) followed by TAX (premium*remaining_terms/12/10) followed by AUDIT (0).
6. negative adjustment: when premium < 0, export CREDIT (-premium).
7. taxable amendment: when transaction equals "AMEND", export DEBIT (premium*remaining_terms/12) followed by TAX (premium*remaining_terms/12/10).
8. inception: when otherwise, export BIND (premium).

Input 0 (In_endorsement_proration_0): proposal_id is required string; transaction is required string; premium is required decimal; remaining_terms is required decimal; reviewed is required boolean; remark is nullable string.
Output 0 (Out_endorsement_proration_0): proposal_ref is required string; posting is required string; amount is required decimal.
Each source ID is unique; carry proposal_id into proposal_ref. Entry labels go in posting, values in amount.

DEBIT and BIND create new premium versions. REFUND and CREDIT retire the prior endorsement and retain prior_endorsement_key. TAX is a supporting entry for the first premium version opened by this event; AUDIT refers to that same version. WAIVER and ERROR have no version identity. Where an annotation refers to an opening, use its version_key; all other unversioned messages use null. A branch producing no postings establishes no versions. The prior identity is supplied on input 0 as prior_endorsement_key (long, non-null). It is never replaced on records concerning that prior version.
Output additions: version_key (long, nullable); opens_version (boolean, required). Mark only fresh versions with true.
Fresh version numbers come from primitive sequence EndorsementVersionSK, whose first value is 4100000500 and increment is 1; reset it for this run. Every opened version needs its own number, including separate openings from one source event.

```ctl
//#CTL2
string endorsement_reference;
string[] endorsement_actions = [];
decimal[] endorsement_values = [];
long[] endorsement_version_keys = [];
boolean[] endorsement_opens = [];
long endorsement_first_open;
long endorsement_last_open;
long endorsement_prior;
function void post_endorsement(string label, decimal value) {
    append(endorsement_actions, label);
    append(endorsement_values, value);
    boolean opening = label == "DEBIT" || label == "BIND";
    long assigned_key = null;
    if (opening) {
        assigned_key = sequence(EndorsementVersionSK, long).next();
        if (endorsement_first_open == null) endorsement_first_open = assigned_key;
        endorsement_last_open = assigned_key;
    } else if (label == "REFUND" || label == "CREDIT") {
        assigned_key = endorsement_prior;
    }
    append(endorsement_version_keys, assigned_key);
