prompt:
Validate this Normalizer transform against its metadata and requirements.

The Normalizer CTL2 for this complete event-posting policy.

For manufacturing inspection and recovery, choose the earliest eligible treatment below. Every treatment lists its complete ordered payload.

[impossible production] eligibility: planned < 0 or actual < 0 or scrap < 0 or scrap > actual; result: ERROR {units=0, quality_grade=null, released=false}.
[missing inspection] eligibility: quality equals null; result: HOLD {units=actual, quality_grade=null, released=false}.
[batch cancellation] eligibility: quality equals "CANCEL"; result: no postings.
[rejected grade without recovery] eligibility: quality equals "REJECT" and not rework_allowed; result: SCRAP {units=actual, quality_grade=quality, released=false}.
[recoverable rejected grade] eligibility: quality equals "REJECT"; result: GOOD {units=accepted/3, quality_grade=quality, released=true}; then REWORK {units=accepted-accepted/3, quality_grade=quality, released=false}; then SCRAP {units=scrap, quality_grade=quality, released=false}.
[reviewed accepted batch] eligibility: review; result: AUDIT {units=0, quality_grade=quality, released=false}; then GOOD {units=accepted, quality_grade=quality, released=true}; then SCRAP {units=scrap, quality_grade=quality, released=false}.
[short production] eligibility: accepted+5 < planned; result: GOOD {units=accepted, quality_grade=quality, released=true}; then SHORT {units=planned-accepted, quality_grade=quality, released=false}.
[ordinary accepted production] eligibility: otherwise; result: GOOD {units=accepted, quality_grade=quality, released=true}; then SCRAP {units=scrap, quality_grade=quality, released=false}.

Let accepted equal actual minus scrap. Divide accepted by three using integer truncation; the second recovery share receives every remaining accepted unit. Thus recoverable GOOD, REWORK and SCRAP conserve actual production. Only GOOD is released; other rows retain the inspected grade, and missing-grade HOLD or ERROR has no grade.

Input 0 Source_manufacturing_2: batch_id / required / string; planned / required / integer; actual / required / integer; scrap / required / integer; quality / nullability omitted / string; rework_allowed / required / boolean; review / required / boolean.
Output 0 Posting_manufacturing_2: source_batch_id / required / string; material_action / required / string; units / required / integer; quality_grade / nullable / string; released / required / boolean.
