Fire door checks require this behavior: Accept the inspection group only when every observation is explicitly true. A missing or false observation rejects it. Before applying that calculation, treat each missing accepted as true. Include the source-record total in observation_count.
Grouping fields: door_id, inspection_stage. Records sharing that full key arrive together, in source order.
Input:
<Record name="AllAcceptedInput" type="delimited" fieldDelimiter=";" recordDelimiter="&#10;"><Field name="door_id" type="string" nullable="false"/><Field name="inspection_stage" type="integer" nullable="false"/><Field name="accepted" type="boolean"/></Record>
Accumulator:
<Record name="AllAcceptedState" type="delimited" fieldDelimiter=";" recordDelimiter="&#10;"><Field name="observations" type="integer" nullable="false"/><Field name="all_ok" type="boolean"/></Record>
Output 0:
<Record name="AllAcceptedSummary" type="delimited" fieldDelimiter=";" recordDelimiter="&#10;"><Field name="door_id" type="string" nullable="false"/><Field name="inspection_stage" type="integer" nullable="false"/><Field name="observation_count" type="integer" nullable="false"/><Field name="result" type="boolean" nullable="true"/></Record>

```ctl
//#CTL2
function void initGroup(AllAcceptedState acc) {
    acc.all_ok = true;
}
function boolean updateGroup(AllAcceptedState acc) {
    acc.observations++;
    if ($in.0.accepted != true) acc.all_ok = false;
    return false;
}
function integer updateTransform(integer counter, AllAcceptedState acc) {
    return SKIP;
}
function boolean finishGroup(AllAcceptedState acc) {
    return true;
}
function integer transform(integer counter, AllAcceptedState acc) {
    if (counter > 0) return SKIP;
    $out.0.door_id = $in.0.door_id;
    $out.0.inspection_stage = $in.0.inspection_stage;
    $out.0.observation_count = acc.observations;
    $out.0.result = acc.all_ok;
    return ALL;
}
```

