Implement the following intake mapping.

Seal intake: copy seal_id; trim seal_text; classify null or empty as MISSING, a whole-string mismatch to [A-Z]{2}[0-9]{4} as INVALID, otherwise VALID. Also output normalized trimmed uppercase text and held, treating null held as false. Count one problem each for non-VALID status, quantity null/nonpositive, priority null/outside 0..9, blank destination, operator code outside OP followed by three digits, and held. Route REVIEW if any problem, else EXPRESS at priority >=7, else STANDARD. Quantity band is UNKNOWN for null, EMPTY at <=0, BULK at >=100, SMALL otherwise. Priority band is UNKNOWN for null, INVALID outside 0..9, HIGH at >=7, NORMAL otherwise. destination_ok means nonblank; operator_ok uses that exact whole-string OP pattern.

