Build the complete component script.

Permit screening: copy permit_id; trim permit_text; classify null or empty as MISSING, a whole-string mismatch to P[0-9]{3}[A-Z] as INVALID, otherwise VALID. Also output normalized trimmed uppercase text and held, treating null held as false. Count one problem each for non-VALID status, quantity null/nonpositive, priority null/outside 0..9, blank destination, operator code outside OP followed by three digits, and held. Route REVIEW if any problem, else EXPRESS at priority >=7, else STANDARD. Quantity band is UNKNOWN for null, EMPTY at <=0, BULK at >=100, SMALL otherwise. Priority band is UNKNOWN for null, INVALID outside 0..9, HIGH at >=7, NORMAL otherwise. destination_ok means nonblank; operator_ok uses that exact whole-string OP pattern.

Component: REFORMAT.
Input 0: {"name": "PermitInput", "type": "delimited", "fields": [{"name": "permit_id", "type": "integer"}, {"name": "permit_text", "type": "string"}, {"name": "quantity", "type": "integer"}, {"name": "priority", "type": "integer"}, {"name": "held", "type": "boolean"}, {"name": "destination", "type": "string"}, {"name": "operator_code", "type": "string"}]}
