prompt:
Validate this Normalizer transform against its metadata and requirements.

Build event expansion for the inventory transfer journals feed, applying the first matching test. Keep listed postings in order.

1) void transfer: qualifying condition ticket equals "VOID"; ordered result nothing.
2) damaged units: qualifying condition requested < 0; ordered result REJECT valued at -requested.
3) same bin: qualifying condition ticket equals "SAME"; ordered result nothing.
4) quarantine: qualifying condition ticket equals "QUARANTINE"; ordered result HOLD valued at requested.
5) short pick: qualifying condition available < requested; ordered result PICK valued at available, then SHORT valued at requested-available.
6) large audited move: qualifying condition requested >= 15 and trace; ordered result OUT valued at -requested, then IN valued at requested, then TRACE valued at 0.
7) ordinary paired move: qualifying condition ticket equals "MOVE"; ordered result OUT valued at -requested, then IN valued at requested.
8) inventory sample: qualifying condition none of the preceding conditions applies; ordered result SAMPLE valued at requested, then RESERVE valued at available.

Input 0 (In_bin_transfer_2): required field external_move_id, represented as string; required field ticket, represented as string; required field requested, represented as decimal; required field available, represented as decimal; required field trace, represented as boolean; nullable field bin_note, represented as string.
Output 0 (Out_bin_transfer_2): required field parent_move_ref, represented as string; required field movement, represented as string; required field units, represented as decimal.
Each source ID is unique; carry external_move_id into parent_move_ref. Entry labels go in movement, values in units.

```ctl
//#CTL2
string bin_reference;
string[] bin_actions = [];
decimal[] bin_values = [];
function void post_bin(string label, decimal value) {
    append(bin_actions, label);
    append(bin_values, value);
}
function integer count() {
    bin_actions = [];
    bin_values = [];
    bin_reference = $in.0.external_move_id;
    /* Priority table:
       1. void transfer -> 0 rows
       2. damaged units -> 1 rows
       3. same bin -> 0 rows
       4. quarantine -> 1 rows
       5. short pick -> 2 rows
       6. large audited move -> 3 rows
       7. ordinary paired move -> 2 rows
       8. inventory sample -> 2 rows
    */
    if ($in.0.ticket == "VOID") {
        return 0; // void transfer
    }
    else if ($in.0.requested < 0d) {
        post_bin("REJECT", -$in.0.requested);
        return 1; // damaged units
    }
    else if ($in.0.ticket == "SAME") {
        return 0; // same bin
    }
    else if ($in.0.ticket == "QUARANTINE") {
        post_bin("HOLD", $in.0.requested);
        return 1; // quarantine
    }
    else if ($in.0.available < $in.0.requested) {
        post_bin("PICK", $in.0.available);
        post_bin("SHORT", $in.0.requested-$in.0.available);
        return 2; // short pick
    }
    else if ($in.0.requested >= 15d && $in.0.trace) {
        post_bin("OUT", -$in.0.requested);
        post_bin("IN", $in.0.requested);
        post_bin("TRACE", 0d);
        return 3; // large audited move
    }
    else if ($in.0.ticket == "MOVE") {
        post_bin("OUT", -$in.0.requested);
        post_bin("IN", $in.0.requested);
        return 2; // ordinary paired move
    }
    else if (true) {
        post_bin("SAMPLE", $in.0.requested);
        post_bin("RESERVE", $in.0.available);
        return 2; // inventory sample
    }
    return 0;
}
function integer transform(integer idx) {
    $out.0.parent_move_ref = bin_reference;
    $out.0.movement = bin_actions[idx];
    $out.0.units = bin_values[idx];
    return ALL;
}
```

