Validate this Normalizer transform against its metadata and requirements.

Build event expansion for the collateral margin instructions feed, applying the first matching test. Keep listed postings in order.

1) instruction equals "CLOSED" means nothing, under the closed agreement treatment.
2) posted < 0 means ERROR valued at -posted, under the bad collateral treatment.
3) instruction equals "TOLERANCE" and exposure-posted*0.8 <= 30 means nothing, under the within tolerance treatment.
4) instruction equals "NOVATE" means RELEASE valued at -posted, then POST valued at exposure/0.8, under the novation treatment.
5) exposure > posted*0.8 and review means EXISTING valued at posted*0.8, then CALL valued at exposure-posted*0.8, then AUDIT valued at 0, under the reviewed shortage treatment.
6) posted*0.8 > exposure means RELEASE valued at exposure/0.8-posted, under the surplus release treatment.
7) exposure > posted*0.8 means CALL valued at exposure-posted*0.8, under the unreviewed shortage treatment.
8) none of the preceding conditions applies means BALANCED valued at 0, under the balanced agreement treatment.

Input 0 (In_collateral_margin_2): external_agreement_event_id [string/required]; instruction [string/required]; exposure [decimal/required]; posted [decimal/required]; review [boolean/required]; agreement_note [string/nullable].
Output 0 (Out_collateral_margin_2): parent_agreement_ref [string/required]; margin_leg [string/required]; amount [decimal/required].
