Write laundry intake audit CTL. Use a Rollup grouped by wash_run, with adjacent groups processed in input order. Input LaundryObservation(wash_run:string, bag_tag:string, received_at:date, weight:decimal, fabric:string). Accumulator metadata is fixed at LaundryAccumulator(sum_value:decimal, seen:integer); all metadata listed here is final. Output LaundrySummary(wash_run:string, first_ref:string, last_ref:string, first_year:integer, last_year:integer, accepted:integer, missing:integer, negative:integer, primary_count:integer, secondary_count:integer, minimum:decimal, maximum:decimal, total:decimal, mean_value:decimal, disposition:string, audit_text:string). Save the first and last bag_tag (including null) and their UTC calendar years; a null timestamp yields a null year. Classify fabric into PRIMARY, SECONDARY or other. Exclude negative and null weight from accepted, min, max, total and mean; zero qualifies. Count missing and negative observations separately. The average is rounded to two places, null without accepted values. Disposition is EMPTY without accepted values, otherwise REVIEW when anything is missing or negative, else READY. Join every bag_tag in encounter order with commas, substituting ? for null. Emit one summary per group, no intermediate rows.

