Validate this Normalizer transform against its metadata and requirements.

Build event expansion for the microgrid energy settlement feed, applying the first matching test. Keep listed postings in order.

1) Test quality equals "OBSOLETE". On success the entries are nothing.
2) Test exported < 0. On success the entries are ERROR valued at -exported.
3) Test imported equals exported. On success the entries are nothing.
4) Test quality equals "ESTIMATE". On success the entries are ESTIMATE valued at imported-exported.
5) Test exported > imported and audit. On success the entries are IMPORT valued at imported, then EXPORT valued at -exported, then AUDIT valued at 0.
6) Test imported > exported and imported-exported < 30. On success the entries are NET valued at imported-exported, then ROUNDING valued at 0.
7) Test exported > imported. On success the entries are EXPORT valued at imported-exported.
8) Test none of the preceding conditions applies. On success the entries are IMPORT valued at imported-exported, then LEVY valued at (imported-exported)/10.

Input 0 (In_energy_netting_2): external_reading_id:string (required); quality:string (required); imported:decimal (required); exported:decimal (required); audit:boolean (required); source_note:string (nullable).
Output 0 (Out_energy_netting_2): parent_reading_ref:string (required); energy_leg:string (required); quantity:decimal (required).
Each source ID is unique; carry external_reading_id into parent_reading_ref. Entry labels go in energy_leg, values in quantity.

```ctl
//#CTL2
string energy_reference;
string[] energy_actions = [];
decimal[] energy_values = [];
function void post_energy(string label, decimal value) {
    append(energy_actions, label);
    append(energy_values, value);
}
function integer count() {
    energy_actions = [];
    energy_values = [];
    energy_reference = $in.0.external_reading_id;
    /* Priority table:
       1. replaced reading -> 0 rows
       2. invalid export -> 1 rows
       3. balanced meter -> 0 rows
       4. estimated interval -> 1 rows
       5. audited export surplus -> 3 rows
       6. small import -> 2 rows
       7. net export -> 1 rows
       8. billable import -> 2 rows
    */
    if ($in.0.quality == "OBSOLETE") {
        return 0; // replaced reading
    }
    else if ($in.0.exported < 0d) {
        post_energy("ERROR", -$in.0.exported);
        return 1; // invalid export
    }
    else if ($in.0.imported == $in.0.exported) {
        return 0; // balanced meter
    }
    else if ($in.0.quality == "ESTIMATE") {
        post_energy("ESTIMATE", $in.0.imported-$in.0.exported);
        return 1; // estimated interval
    }
    else if ($in.0.exported > $in.0.imported && $in.0.audit) {
        post_energy("IMPORT", $in.0.imported);
        post_energy("EXPORT", -$in.0.exported);
        post_energy("AUDIT", 0d);
        return 3; // audited export surplus
    }
    else if ($in.0.imported > $in.0.exported && $in.0.imported-$in.0.exported < 30d) {
        post_energy("NET", $in.0.imported-$in.0.exported);
        post_energy("ROUNDING", 0d);
        return 2; // small import
    }
    else if ($in.0.exported > $in.0.imported) {
        post_energy("EXPORT", $in.0.imported-$in.0.exported);
        return 1; // net export
    }
    else if (true) {
        post_energy("IMPORT", $in.0.imported-$in.0.exported);
        post_energy("LEVY", ($in.0.imported-$in.0.exported)/10d);
        return 2; // billable import
    }
    return 0;
}
function integer transform(integer idx) {
    $out.0.parent_reading_ref = energy_reference;
    $out.0.energy_leg = energy_actions[idx];
    $out.0.quantity = energy_values[idx];
    return ALL;
}
