Transform weavery loom run observations. Use a Rollup grouped by loom_run, with adjacent groups processed in input order. Input WeaveryObservation(loom_run:string, spool_ref:string, mounted_at:date, thread_length:decimal, fiber:string). Accumulator metadata is fixed at WeaveryAccumulator(sum_value:decimal, seen:integer); all metadata listed here is final. Output WeaverySummary(loom_run:string, first_ref:string, last_ref:string, first_year:integer, last_year:integer, accepted:integer, missing:integer, negative:integer, primary_count:integer, secondary_count:integer, minimum:decimal, maximum:decimal, total:decimal, mean_value:decimal, disposition:string, audit_text:string). Save the first and last spool_ref (including null) and their UTC calendar years; a null timestamp yields a null year. Classify fiber into PRIMARY, SECONDARY or other. Exclude negative and null thread_length from accepted, min, max, total and mean; zero qualifies. Count missing and negative observations separately. The average is rounded to two places, null without accepted values. Disposition is EMPTY without accepted values, otherwise REVIEW when anything is missing or negative, else READY. Join every spool_ref in encounter order with commas, substituting ? for null. Emit one summary per group, no intermediate rows.

