The Normalizer CTL2 for this complete event-posting policy.

For dated escrow approval and release, choose the earliest eligible treatment below. Every treatment lists its complete ordered payload.

[invalid net funding] eligibility: funding < 0 or fee < 0 or net < 0; result: ERROR {amount=0, pay_on=requested_on, final_payment=false}.
[approval unresolved] eligibility: approved equals null; result: PENDING {amount=net, pay_on=requested_on, final_payment=false}.
[approval denied] eligibility: approved equals false; result: no postings.
[not yet due] eligibility: requested_on < due_on; result: no postings.
[reviewed payable release] eligibility: review; result: AUDIT {amount=0, pay_on=requested_on, final_payment=false}; then BENEFICIARY {amount=net*(100-30)/100, pay_on=release_on, final_payment=true}; then RETAIN {amount=net*30/100, pay_on=due_on, final_payment=false}.
[ordinary payable release] eligibility: otherwise; result: BENEFICIARY {amount=net, pay_on=release_on, final_payment=true}; then FEE {amount=fee, pay_on=requested_on, final_payment=false}.

Compute net as funding minus fee and compare dates as UTC instants. Unknown approval remains PENDING; denied or premature requests are suppressed by their listed treatments. A nonsilent event shares one new allocation_key from primitive Keys_escrow_release (long, start 3000000000, increment 1, reset for this run), regardless of package length.

